std:sql.documentation:
SQL failure with code and message. Async operations throw this value at await; row accessors return it in Result. Query/execute errors include the database code when available. Migration codes distinguish invalid source (migration-source), changed or missing applied SQL (migration-drift), partial unfinished migrations (migration-dirty), and execution failures (migration-failed).

```tsrust
import { SqlError } from "std:sql";

function main() {
  const error: SqlError = {
    code: "column", message: "Missing column"
  };
  console.log(error.code);
  console.log(error.message);
}

// column
// Missing column
```

Ownership: The error owns its strings. Inspect them by borrowing; clone a string to retain an independent copy.

