SqlSqlError.documentation:
Identifies the failure category as a string, such as column, type, range, precision, closed or acquire-timeout. Read this property to choose recovery behavior. Reading takes no arguments, does not mutate the error and does not throw.

```tsrust
import { SqlError } from "std:sql";

function main() {
  const error: SqlError = {
    code: "column", message: "Missing column"
  };
  console.log(error.code);
  console.log(error.message);
}
// column
// Missing column
```

Ownership: reading borrows the error and its string; clone the string to retain an independent value.

