SqlSqlError.documentation:
Describes the failure as a string. Database failures include SQLSTATE when available; exact detail depends on the driver and failure. Use code for category checks. Reading takes no arguments, does not mutate the error and does not throw.

```tsrust
import { connect } from "std:sql";

async function main(): Task<void> {
  const db = await connect("sqlite::memory:", 1);
  const rows = await db.query("SELECT 1 AS id");

  match (rows[0].text("name")) {
    Ok(value) => {
      console.log(value);
    },
    Err(error) => {
      console.log(error.code, error.message.length > 0);
    }
  }

  await db.close();
}
// prints: column true
```

Log the message for operators; branch on `code`.

Ownership: reading borrows the error and its string; clone the string to retain an independent value.

