std:sqlite.documentation:
SQLite operation failure with code and message. busy and locked mean contention; constraint means integrity failure; parameters, type and column identify binding/reading errors. transaction-ended means SQLite already rolled back; closed prevents reuse after failed rollback.

```tsrust
import { SqliteError } from "std:sqlite";

function main() {
  const error: SqliteError = {
    code: "column", message: "Missing column"
  };
  console.log(error.code);
  console.log(error.message);
}

// column
// Missing column
```

Ownership: The error owns its strings. Inspect them by borrowing; clone a string to retain an independent copy.

