SqliteConnection.documentation:
Begins an IMMEDIATE transaction, acquiring the write reservation now. Lock contention returns busy/locked after the configured wait. Returns Result with SqliteError on failure; unwrap propagates the error to try/catch.

```tsrust
const tx = unwrap(db.begin());
// Prepare and execute statements through tx.
unwrap(tx.commit());
```

Ownership: exclusively borrows the connection. Until finished, use the transaction instead of the connection. Dropping it or throwing before commit rolls it back.

examples.source:
import { open } from 'std:sqlite';

function main(): void {
  const db = unwrap(open(':memory:'));
  {
    const create = unwrap(db.prepare('CREATE TABLE accounts(balance INTEGER)'));
    unwrap(create.execute());
  }
  try {
    const transaction = unwrap(db.begin());
    const insert = unwrap(transaction.prepare('INSERT INTO accounts VALUES (?1)'));
    unwrap(insert.execute([100]));
    throw 'Transfer failed'; // Leaving this scope rolls the transaction back.
  } catch (error) {
    if (typeof error === 'string') {
      console.log(error);
    } else {
      console.log(error.message);
    }
  }
  {
    const count = unwrap(db.prepare('SELECT count(*) AS total FROM accounts'));
    const rows = unwrap(count.query());
    console.log(unwrap(rows[0].int('total'))); // 0
  }
  unwrap(db.close());
}

