Creates a reusable pool of worker threads. `new ThreadPool()` uses one worker per available CPU (at least 1) and allows 1024 outstanding tasks.

@param options - Set both `workers` and `capacity` (positive integers). Capacity counts queued, running and finished-but-uncollected tasks. Invalid values throw `SpawnError` code `range`; failure to start workers throws code `spawn`.

Limits are fixed once created; there is no global pool. `shutdown` closes the pool for good. At scope exit the pool finishes queued and running work, including detached tasks.

Ownership: one owner, not cloneable; pass it around or borrow it as `ReadOnly<ThreadPool>`. Worker callbacks cannot capture it.

```tsrust
