```tsrust
import { compile, escape } from 'std:regex';

function main() {
  const value = unwrap(compile('(é)(x)?'));
  console.log('é é'.matchAll(value).length);
}
```

Expected output: 2.

Ownership: matching borrows the compiled owner and input only during the call. Returned ranges, capture arrays and strings are independently owned.

Returns the byte offset of the first match using a compiled Regex, or -1 if absent. An empty pattern matches at offset zero. No receiver mutation or implicit compilation occurs.

```tsrust
import { compile, escape } from 'std:regex';

