Reusable locale-sensitive comparison returns -1,0 or1 and leaves inputs unchanged. Unset options preserve locale defaults, including tertiary strength normally. Numeric ordering and case-first preferences may be supplied through locale Unicode keywords. Data lookup uses backend locale fallback; default compiled data does not include search collations.

```tsrust
import { parseLocale, formatLocale, createCollator, createSegmenter, createNumberFormat } from 'std:locale';

function main() {
  const locale = unwrap(parseLocale('en-u-kn-true'));
  const value = unwrap(createCollator(locale));
  console.log('2'.localeCompare('10', value));
}
```

Expected output: -1.

Ownership: owners and inputs are borrowed during calls. Returned text and range arrays own their storage.

