Appended/removed owned elements transfer ownership.

Returns `true` when `value` occurs in the array. `NaN` matches `NaN`, and `0` matches `-0`. Works on `int[]`, `number[]`, `boolean[]`, `string[]` and primitive-union arrays.

@param value - The value to find, of the element type (for an array of a primitive union such as `(int | string)[]`, one of its alternatives; ints and numbers compare by value). A union-typed value is an error; narrow it first.
@param fromIndex - Where to start, default `0`; negative counts from the end.

```tsrust
const values: int[] = [1, 2, 3];
console.log(values.includes(2), values.includes(2, 2)); // prints "true false"
```

```tsrust
const mixed: (int | string | null)[] = [1, "two", null];
console.log(mixed.includes("two"), mixed.includes(null), mixed.includes(2)); // prints "true true false"
```

Arrays of records or nested arrays are not supported; use `some()` with a predicate.

