Compares supported structural data recursively using exact scalar values. Numbers treat NaN as equal and distinguish signed zero; integers retain all64bits. Arrays and tuples compare ordered elements, records compare declared fields, and data unions compare matching active alternatives. Maps compare values using existing key lookup semantics, and sets compare membership regardless of insertion order. Callable and opaque native payloads are compile-time errors, including nested payloads. Returns void without mutating inputs. Failure raises AssertionError with the optional message (default "Expected data to be deeply equal").

```tsrust
import { deepStrictEqual } from 'std:testing';

function main() {
  deepStrictEqual([[1, 2]], [[1, 2]]);
}
```

Ownership: both values and the optional message are borrowed. No cloning or serialization is used for comparison.

Fails when supported structural data compares deeply equal. Uses the same scalar, record, array, union, Map and Set rules as deepStrictEqual. Returns void without changing either input. The optional message defaults to "Expected data to differ deeply". Unsupported callable or opaque payloads are compile-time errors.

```tsrust
import { notDeepStrictEqual } from 'std:testing';

function main() {
  notDeepStrictEqual([1, 2], [1, 3]);
}
```

Ownership: both values and the message are borrowed.

Runs the task factory once and passes only if the task throws. The thrown value is discarded, whatever it is. If the task completes normally, throws `AssertionError` with `message` (default "Expected task to reject").

```tsrust
import { rejects } from 'std:testing';
async function main(): Task<void> {
  await rejects(async () => {
    throw {
      code: 'expected'
    };
  });
}
```

A panic or cancellation in an awaited `Job` counts as a throw. Cancelling the `rejects` task itself does not pass the assertion.

Ownership: consumes the factory and `message`.

Calls a synchronous callback exactly once and succeeds if any value is thrown. A normal return causes AssertionError with the optional message, default "Expected function to throw". Returns void and does not retain the callback. The caught value is discarded; no error matcher or coercion is performed. Async callbacks do not match the signature, and asynchronous work is not awaited. Callback-local resources use ordinary checked exception cleanup. The assertion's own failure occurs outside its catch.

```tsrust
import { throws } from "std:testing";

function main() {
  throws(() => {
    throw "expected";
  });
  console.log("passed");
}
// passed
```

Ownership: consumes the single-use callback, including owned captures; the message is borrowed. The callback cannot be reused after passing it.

Calls a synchronous callback once and returns the console standard output it wrote, in order, as one string. Output written while capturing is not printed. console.error and other standard-error output are not captured. Nested captures return only their own text. If the callback throws, capture ends, its partial output is discarded and the exception propagates.

```tsrust
import { captureOutput, strictEqual } from "std:testing";

function main() {
  const text = captureOutput(() => {
    console.log("a");
    console.log(1, 2);
  });
  strictEqual(text, "a\n1 2\n");
  console.log("passed");
}
```

Expected output: passed.

Use it to assert a program's exact output in a consolidated test suite. Asynchronous work that prints after the callback returns is not captured.

Ownership: consumes the single-use callback; the returned string is owned.

Starts capturing console standard output on the current test's thread. Pair it with finishOutputCapture(), which returns the captured text. Use the pair instead of captureOutput when the measured code can throw or await: errors propagate normally, and the runner discards an unfinished capture before the next test. Captures nest.

```tsrust
import { startOutputCapture, finishOutputCapture, strictEqual } from "std:testing";

function main() {
  startOutputCapture();
  console.log("a");
  strictEqual(finishOutputCapture(), "a\n");
  console.log("passed");
}
```

Expected output: passed.

Ownership: takes no arguments and returns void.

