Changes an open file length without moving its current cursor. Shrinking discards trailing bytes; extending makes added bytes read as zero. Writes after shrinking begin at the unchanged cursor, possibly creating a hole. A readonly handle returns FsError; no durability synchronization occurs. Returns Ok with the result, or Err(FsError) for filesystem failures; message and osCode may vary by platform. Ownership: mutably borrows the handle; it remains open after success or failure.

