std:bytes.documentation:
An owned, growable byte buffer; each element is 0 to 255. Lengths count bytes, not characters.

Create one with `fromArray` or `alloc`. Read with `length` and `at`, write with `set`, grow with `append` and `resize`. `copy` copies a range and `clone(bytes)` copies all of it. Buffers cannot be printed, compared, spread or built with record literals.

```tsrust
import { fromUtf8, length, at, set, toUtf8 } from "std:bytes";

function main() {
  const bytes = unwrap(fromUtf8("hi"));
  console.log(length(bytes), unwrap(at(bytes, 0)));
  unwrap(set(bytes, 0, 72)); // "H"
  console.log(unwrap(toUtf8(bytes)));
}
// prints: 2 104
// prints: Hi
```

Ownership: passing a buffer by value moves it; `ReadOnly<Bytes>` borrows it without copying.

