Adds `values` to the end of the buffer, in order. Each value must be 0 to 255; nothing is wrapped. An empty array changes nothing. Every failure keeps the original length and contents.

Returns `Ok()`, or an error with no change: `byte-range` with the bad value's index as `offset`, `length-range` if the total length is too large, `allocation` if memory cannot be reserved.

