Returns new `Bytes` with a copy of bytes `start` up to (not including) `end`. `start` equal to `end` gives an empty buffer. Changing either buffer later does not affect the other. The result is an independent owned buffer.

Bounds must satisfy `0 <= start <= end <= length(bytes)`; negative values do not count from the end and nothing is clamped. An invalid range returns code `range` with the first bad bound as `offset`. A reversed range reports `end`. Failure to reserve memory returns `allocation`.

```tsrust
