Returns a read-only window onto bytes `start` up to (not including) `end`, without copying. `start` equal to `end` gives an empty view. Positions in a view of a view are relative to that view. The result is a readonly window.

Bounds must satisfy `0 <= start <= end <= length(bytes)`; negative values do not count from the end and nothing is clamped. An invalid range returns code `range` with the first bad bound as `offset`. A reversed range reports `end`. A range that splits a character makes `toUtf8` of the view fail.

```tsrust
import { fromUtf8, view, toUtf8 } from "std:bytes";

function main() {
  match (fromUtf8("hello")) {
    Ok(bytes) => {
      match (view(bytes, 1, 4)) {
        Ok(part) => {
          match (toUtf8(part)) {
            Ok(text) => {
              console.log(text);
            },
            Err(error) => {
              console.log(error.message);
            },
          }
        },
        Err(error) => {
          console.log(error.message);
        },
