Calls `callback` with `(value, key, map)` for each entry in key order. The callback may take fewer parameters; its return value is ignored. An empty map makes no calls. Errors thrown by the callback propagate.

```tsrust
import { OrderedMap } from "std:collections";

function main() {
  const values = new OrderedMap<string, int>();
