Construction budgets with required int fields maxDepth, maxEntries and maxNodes. Omitted or undefined limits impose no construction quota; Rust allocation and stack limits apply. Explicit limits must be nonnegative integers that fit this platform; maxDepth has no fixed upper quota. The root counts as one value and one container level. maxEntries applies to every nested collection; maxNodes counts the root and all descendant values. Zero entries permits an empty container; zero depth or nodes rejects any container. Errors use depth-limit, entry-limit, node-limit or invalid-limits with offset zero. Existing inputs are already allocated; these limits bound the resulting tree, not an input byte stream. No receiver is mutated. Ownership: ordinary owned record, borrowed by constructors.

