Borrows an existing `BufferedReader` to read JSON Lines from its current position, reusing its buffer. `readJsonl` and `readJsonl<T>` accept it; `undefined` marks the end, distinct from JSON `null`. Omitted limits impose no per-record quota; LF is not counted in `maxBytes`. A read failure is terminal. Error line and offset count from where the view started. Closing it (or leaving scope) leaves the reader open with unread bytes preserved. Omitted limits impose no per-record byte, entry or node quota.

```tsrust
import { fromUtf8, toUtf8 } from "std:bytes";
import { open, bufferReader, read, close, writeFile } from "std:fs";
import { borrowJsonl, readJsonl } from "std:json";

function main() {
  unwrap(writeFile("mixed.txt", unwrap(fromUtf8("v1\n1\n2\n"))));
  const input = unwrap(bufferReader(unwrap(open("mixed.txt"))));
  console.log(unwrap(toUtf8(unwrap(read(input, 3))))); // a plain-text header line
  {
    const records = unwrap(borrowJsonl(input)); // continues from the current position
    while (true) {
      const value = unwrap(readJsonl<int>(records));

      if (value === undefined) break;
      console.log(value);
    }
  }

  unwrap(close(input));
}
// prints: v1 (followed by the newline that was read with it)
// prints: 1
// prints: 2
```

Ownership: exclusively borrows the buffered reader; the reader cannot be used, moved or closed while the view is live, and the view cannot be cloned or escape. Close the reader yourself afterwards.

