One owned name/value pair decoded by request.form(). Both fields are strings. Duplicate names remain separate array elements in input order; plus signs decode to spaces and percent escapes are decoded.

The example prints 'body one two'.

```tsrust
import { request, FormField } from 'std:http';
async function main(): Task<void> {
  const form = request('POST', 'http://localhost/', 'body=one+two');
  form.setHeader('content-type', 'application/x-www-form-urlencoded');
  const fields: FormField[] = await form.form();
  console.log(fields[0].name, fields[0].value);
}
```

Ownership: the decoded field owns its strings independently of the request body.

