std:http.documentation:
Creates a response whose body is the byte chunks sent on `channel`, without collecting them first. Sends wait when the channel is full; capacity counts chunks, not bytes, so keep chunks small.

The body ends when every sender is dropped and queued chunks are sent. If the client disconnects, pending sends fail with code `closed`. An invalid `status` throws code `status`. The producer task is yours to keep running, and you choose how to report its errors. No `Content-Type` is set.

```tsrust
const producer = produce(chunks.sender()).start();

try {
  const response = streamChannel(chunks);
  await response.text();
} finally {
  await producer;
}
```

Ownership: consumes the channel; senders stay usable until the response closes.

