HttpApp.documentation:
Starts the server when awaited: binds `address`, stops further route registration and returns the running `Server`. `TlsOptions` failures surface during the TLS handshake; clients check the certificate hostname.

@param tls - Omit for plain HTTP. Pass `{ cert, key }` for HTTPS (HTTP/1.1 and HTTP/2): `cert` is a PEM certificate chain, leaf first; `key` its unencrypted PEM private key (PKCS#1, PKCS#8 or SEC1).

Bad TLS settings throw `HttpError` code `tls` before binding; a bad address or bind failure throws code `address` or `listen`. Body, connection, concurrency and deadline limits apply only if `configure` was called.

```tsrust
const server = await app.listen("127.0.0.1:0", {
  cert: certificatePem, key: privateKeyPem
});
```

Ownership: consumes the app and TLS options. Dropping the `Server` shuts it down after in-flight requests finish.

Sets server limits before `listen`. All seven fields are required: `bodyLimit`, `maxConnections` and `maxRequests` (positive), three positive millisecond deadlines, and `requestsPerSecond` (0 disables rate limiting). Invalid values throw `HttpError` code `options` and keep the previous settings. Without `configure`, no limits beyond the transport defaults apply.

Responses when limits are hit: too many concurrent handlers 503; rate limit 429 with `Retry-After: 1` (a global one-second window, not per user); handler deadline 504 (the handler is asked to cancel); a body over `bodyLimit` 413. Extra connections wait in the OS backlog.

```tsrust
app.configure({
  bodyLimit: 65536, maxConnections: 64, maxRequests: 32, requestTimeoutMs: 5000, shutdownTimeoutMs: 5000, handshakeTimeoutMs: 3000, requestsPerSecond: 100
});
```

Ownership: borrows `options`.

HttpRequest.documentation:
Reads the request body as JSON when awaited and returns a `JsonValue`. Use `schema.parse(await request.json())` to get a validated record. `Content-Type` is ignored.

Empty, malformed or trailing input throws `JsonError` (code, message, byte offset); body or UTF-8 failures throw `HttpError`. JSON input is limited to 16777216 bytes, depth 64 and 1000000 entries.

```tsrust
const schema = s.object({
  name: s.string()
});
const value = schema.parse(await c.req.json());
return c.text(value.name); // hello for {"name":"hello"}
```

The body can be read only once, even if parsing fails; later reads throw `HttpError` code `body`.

Ownership: the request moves into the task (for `c.req`, the context is borrowed until it settles); the result owns its data.

examples.source:
import {App, request, ServerOptions, FormField, MultipartPart} from 'std:http';
import {length} from 'std:bytes';
async function main(): Task<void> {
  const options: ServerOptions = {bodyLimit: 65536, maxConnections: 64, maxRequests: 32, requestTimeoutMs: 5000, shutdownTimeoutMs: 5000, handshakeTimeoutMs: 3000, requestsPerSecond: 100};
  const app = new App();
  app.configure(options);
  console.log(options.bodyLimit, options.maxConnections, options.maxRequests, options.requestTimeoutMs, options.shutdownTimeoutMs, options.handshakeTimeoutMs, options.requestsPerSecond);
  const form = request('POST', 'http://localhost/', 'body=one+two');
  form.setHeader('content-type', 'application/x-www-form-urlencoded');
  const fields: FormField[] = await form.form();
  console.log(fields[0].name, fields[0].value);
  const upload = request('POST', 'http://localhost/', '--x\r\nContent-Disposition: form-data; name="attachment"; filename="../untrusted"\r\nContent-Type: application/octet-stream\r\n\r\nabc\r\n--x--\r\n');
  upload.setHeader('content-type', 'multipart/form-data; boundary=x');
  const parts: MultipartPart[] = await upload.multipart();
  console.log(parts[0].name, parts[0].fileName === '../untrusted', parts[0].contentType === 'application/octet-stream', length(parts[0].data));
}

HttpRequest.documentation:
Returns the first value for a decoded, case-sensitive query name, or undefined when absent. Bare keys and empty values return empty strings. Decodes + as space and valid percent-encoded UTF-8 once. Undecodable consecutive escape runs remain literal; no replacement characters or numeric conversion. Empty names are ignored. The name argument is required. No receiver mutation or body consumption.

```tsrust
import { request } from "std:http";

function main() {
  const input = request("GET", "http://localhost/?tag=a+b&tag=c", "");
  const value = input.query("tag");

  if (value !== undefined) {
    console.log(value);
  }
}
```

Expected output: a b.

Ownership: borrows the request and returns independent owned text.

Returns every value for a decoded, case-sensitive query name in wire order, or undefined when absent. Bare keys and empty values return empty strings. Decodes + as space and valid percent-encoded UTF-8 once. Undecodable consecutive escape runs remain literal; no replacement characters or numeric conversion. Empty names are ignored. The name argument is required. No receiver mutation or body consumption.

```tsrust
import { request } from "std:http";

function main() {
  const input = request("GET", "http://localhost/?tag=a+b&tag=c", "");
  const values = input.queries("tag");

  if (values !== undefined) {
    console.log(values.join(","));
  }
}
```

