function main() {
  const cache = new LruCache<string, string>(2);

  match (cache.set("a", "one", 0)) {
    Ok(_) => {
      console.log("stored");
    },
    Err(error) => {
      console.log(error.code, error.key, error.value);
    }
  }
}
// prints: ttl a one
```

Ownership: The record owns its fields. Explicit clone is available only when every field supports independent cloning. Resource fields cannot be cloned. No implicit sharing or cloning occurs.

Creates a least-recently-used cache, bounded by entry count, that can be shared between tasks and threads with `share()`. `capacity` must be positive (otherwise `RangeError`). Keys are one numeric, boolean, string or enum type; values must be cloneable owned data.

Each call is atomic, but `get` followed by `set` is not a transaction. Entries do not expire in the background.

