Ownership: The cache is uniquely owned and cannot be cloned or transferred to a worker. Non-copy values borrow read-only storage and retain an exclusive cache-owner loan until last use; no further cache operation or owner transfer is allowed during that loan. Copy scalars are independent snapshots. Last-use release applies to acyclic local bodies; loops, deferred callbacks, named capture plans and exception regions retain the lexical boundary, so use an inner block there. Use explicit clone(value) when supported, or remove to transfer ownership.

