function main() {
  const cache = new SharedLruCache<string, string>(2);
  unwrap(cache.set("a", "one"));
  const value = cache.getCloned("a");
  cache.clear();

  if (value !== undefined) {
    console.log(value);
  }
}
```

Expected output: one.

Ownership: Handles share one bounded cache only through explicit share(). Operations serialize internally and release the lock before returning; no borrowed value or lock crosses suspension. The final handle releases remaining entries. Independent clone(cache) is rejected.

Purges expired entries, looks up the key, and preserves recency. Missing or expired keys return undefined. A hit returns an independent owned copy, including nested data. Reading never extends the insertion TTL. Takes one key of the declared type. The returned value remains valid after another operation or handle destruction.

```tsrust
