Extracts and expands SHA256 key material into exactly length owned bytes. Zero returns empty Bytes. The 8160-byte maximum is the HKDF algorithm bound, not an application policy. Returns CryptoError Range for invalid lengths; ordinary allocation failure is not a catchable crypto error.

