std:signals.documentation:
Unique subscription to Unix SIGINT/SIGTERM or Windows console SIGINT/SIGBREAK. Register with listen; wait with receive. No clone or transport to concurrent HTTP handlers.

```tsrust
import { listen, receive } from "std:signals";

async function main(): Task<void> {
  const signals = unwrap(listen());
  console.log("ready");
  // A real service awaits this; here a zero deadline ends the wait at once.
  try {
    console.log(await receive(signals).timeout(0));
  } catch (error) {
    console.log(error.code);
  }
}
// prints: ready
// prints: timeout
```

Register before announcing readiness so a shutdown request sent right after startup is not missed.

