HttpContext.documentation:
Constructs a JSON response using pending context headers. Optional status is 200 through 599; omitting it or passing undefined uses c.status(), initially 200. Another status throws HttpError code status. Does not consume or finalize the context; return this response from the handler. JSON serialization rejects unsupported or nonfinite values. 

```tsrust
return c.json({
  message: 'ok'
});
```

Returns status 200 unless previously changed. Ownership: borrows the context; owns the response body.

The checked serializer adds no implicit one-MiB output ceiling. For a bounded serialization operation, use JSON.tryStringify(value,maxBytes) or JSON.stringify(value,maxBytes); explicit limits and data/number errors remain enforced.

