std:regex.documentation:
A reusable compiled Unicode regular expression. Compile once and borrow for repeated searches. No lastIndex state, implicit recompilation or mutation occurs. Supports Rust regex syntax, including inline flags and named groups; lookaround and backreferences are rejected. Empty matches progress on UTF-8 boundaries. The owner is opaque and cannot be constructed or cloned directly.

```tsrust
import { compile, escape } from 'std:regex';

function main() {
  const value = unwrap(compile('(é)(x)?'));
  console.log(value.isMatch('é'));
}
```

Expected output: true.

Ownership: matching borrows the compiled owner and input only during the call. Returned ranges, capture arrays and strings are independently owned.

An independently owned half-open UTF-8 byte range [start,end). start equals end for an empty match. Ranges describe the searched text but retain no text; do not apply them to another input.

```tsrust
import { compile, escape } from 'std:regex';

function main() {
  const value = unwrap(compile('(é)(x)?'));
  console.log(value.findAll('aé')[0].start, value.findAll('aé')[0].end);
}
```

Expected output: 1 3.

Ownership: matching borrows the compiled owner and input only during the call. Returned ranges, capture arrays and strings are independently owned.

The full match and numbered optional capture ranges. groups[n-1] is capture n; group zero is stored once in match. An unmatched group is undefined; an empty matched group has equal start/end offsets. Named groups occupy their ordinary numeric slot; names are not copied into results.

```tsrust
import { compile, escape } from 'std:regex';

function main() {
  const value = unwrap(compile('(é)(x)?'));
  const rows = value.capturesAll('é');
  console.log(rows[0].match.end, rows[0].groups.length);
}
```

Expected output: 2 2.

Ownership: matching borrows the compiled owner and input only during the call. Returned ranges, capture arrays and strings are independently owned.

An owned compile failure. Codes are Syntax, SizeLimit, Range and Compile. message describes the failure and can include pattern text; avoid logging sensitive patterns. Matching an already compiled expression does not return this error.

```tsrust
