Adapts an owned writable resource to a Writer. BufferedWriter retains its pending bytes and writes them in order before later data. Construction performs no write.

Ownership: The destination transfers into the writer.

```tsrust
import { fromUtf8, toUtf8 } from 'std:bytes';
import { createTempDir, create, readFile, removeDirAll } from 'std:fs';
import {
  reader,
  writer,
  write,
  writeAll,
  flush,
  copy,
  close
} from 'std:io';
async function main(): Task<void> {
  const directory = unwrap(createTempDir(undefined, 'io-example-'));
  const path = directory + '/bytes';
  const output = writer(unwrap(create(path)));
  unwrap(await writeAll(output, unwrap(fromUtf8('ok'))));
  unwrap(await flush(output));
  unwrap(await close(output));
  console.log(unwrap(toUtf8(unwrap(readFile(path)))));
  unwrap(removeDirAll(directory));
}
```
Expected stdout: 'ok\n'.

