Copies from `reader` to `writer` until end of stream and returns the number of bytes copied. `bufferSize` sets the working buffer size. With `maxBytes`, it copies that many bytes and returns `limit` if more input remains (one extra byte is read to detect it). Errors and cancellation keep progress made so far. Does not flush or close either side.

```tsrust
import { fromUtf8, toUtf8 } from 'std:bytes';
import { createTempDir, create, readFile, removeDirAll } from 'std:fs';
import {
  reader,
  writer,
  write,
  writeAll,
  flush,
  copy,
  close
} from 'std:io';
async function main(): Task<void> {
  const directory = unwrap(createTempDir(undefined, 'io-example-'));
  const path = directory + '/bytes';
  const output = writer(unwrap(create(path)));
  const input = reader(unwrap(fromUtf8('ok')));
  console.log(unwrap(await copy(input, output, 1)));
  unwrap(await close(input));
  unwrap(await close(output));
  console.log(unwrap(toUtf8(unwrap(readFile(path)))));
  unwrap(removeDirAll(directory));
}
```
Expected stdout: '2\nok\n'.

Either side may also be a full `TcpStream` (not the same stream on both sides) or a compression transform; with a transform, errors add `CompressionError | SpawnError | ThreadError<undefined>`. Finish or close transforms yourself after copying.

Ownership: borrows both sides until the task settles.

