std:process.documentation:
An owned direct OS child. Inspect id while live, transfer each configured pipe once with takeStdin/takeStdout/takeStderr, and await wait or kill. Cancellation of a borrowed wait leaves this retained owner alive. Dropping an unsettled child schedules termination and wait in the current task scope, with kill-on-drop as a backstop. Outside a live runtime, destructor cleanup is best effort. This does not supervise or terminate a whole process tree.

Ownership: unique nonclonable Send owner. Borrowed operations retain their loans until task settlement.

```tsrust
import { args, currentExe } from 'std:env';
import { spawn } from 'std:process';
async function main(): Task<void> {
  if (unwrap(args()).length > 0) {
    return;
  }

  const child = unwrap(spawn(unwrap(currentExe()), ['--child'], {
    stdout: 'null', stderr: 'null'
  }));
  console.log(child.id() !== undefined);
  console.log(unwrap(await child.wait()).success, child.id() === undefined);
  console.log(unwrap(child.tryWait()) !== undefined);
}
```

Expected output:
```text
true
true true
true
```

