std:process.documentation:
Creates a direct child immediately in an active async runtime, inheriting all stdio unless changed explicitly. Args exclude the program name. Bind each child setting locally; parent cwd/environment are unchanged. A synchronous context without a runtime returns code runtime. No shell is inserted. Program and each argument are separate UTF-8 strings. There is no implicit timeout or output limit. ProcessError preserves code, operation, message and optional OS code.

Ownership: borrows program, arguments and options only for this call; returns a unique child. Spawn rejects run-only input/deadline/output options without consuming borrowed resources.

```tsrust
