    Err(error) => console.log(error.code)
  }
}
```

Expected output:
```text
not-found
```

Starts `program` with `args`, writes any `input`, collects stdout and stderr and waits for it to exit. No shell is used, and each argument is passed as is. A non-zero exit status still returns `Ok(Output)`.

There is no timeout or output limit unless set in `options`; hitting one, or cancelling, stops the child and waits for it. Grandchild processes holding the pipes open can delay completion.

Ownership: consumes `options`; borrows `program` and `args` until the task settles. A task never awaited starts nothing.

