std:dns.documentation:
Resolves `host` to IP addresses using the system resolver. `family` (`any`, `ipv4` or `ipv6`, default `any`) filters the results, which may leave an empty array; it does not choose DNS record types. Order and duplicates are as the resolver returns them. An IP address returns itself.

No cache, retry, timeout or limit is added; resolver failures return `NetError`. Cancelling stops waiting, though the OS lookup may continue.

Ownership: borrows `host` and `family` until the task settles; the addresses are new values.

```tsrust
import { lookup } from 'std:dns';
import { formatIp } from 'std:net';
async function main(): Task<void> {
  const addresses = unwrap(await lookup('127.0.0.1'));
  console.log(addresses.length, formatIp(addresses[0]));
  const absent = unwrap(await lookup('127.0.0.1', 'ipv6'));
  console.log(absent.length);
}
```
Expected output:
```text
1 127.0.0.1
0
```

