```

Ownership: The error is owned; reading this finite literal value does not consume its other fields or any transform.

operation.documentation:
Names the operation or validation stage that reported this failure. This is an owned string with no default; buffer operations use their operation label, while stream option validation can report compression or decompress. It is diagnostic context, not a promise that every stage uses the public function name. Reading it does not mutate the error, resume work or return partial output. Use code to classify failures.

```tsrust
