HttpSseEvent.documentation:
Required UTF8 event data. Each CR and LF is preserved as a separate backend line separator, so CRLF becomes two data-line breaks. Empty data writes no data field and alone dispatches no browser event. No Tsrust event-size cap is added. The record and its text are consumed when the channel event is encoded.

```tsrust
import { SseEvent } from "std:http";

function main() {
  const value: SseEvent = {
    data: 'hello'
  };
  console.log(value.data);
}
```

Expected output: hello.

Optional event name. Omitted writes no event field; a browser treats an absent or empty name as message. CR or LF causes a body error when this queued event is encoded, after any preceding bytes. The record is consumed; the receiver is not mutated.

```tsrust
import { SseEvent } from "std:http";

function main() {
  const value: SseEvent = {
    data: 'hello', event: 'update'
  };
  console.log(value.event);
}
```

Expected output: update.

Optional browser last-event identifier. Omitted writes no id field; empty resets the browser identifier. CR, LF and NUL fail when the body reaches this event. Prior headers cannot be changed. The string moves with its event.

```tsrust
import { SseEvent } from "std:http";

function main() {
  const value: SseEvent = {
    data: 'hello', id: '42'
  };
  console.log(value.id);
}
```

Expected output: 42.

Optional nonnegative retry hint in milliseconds; zero is valid and omission writes no retry field. Negative values fail when this event is encoded. This is a client retry hint; the server does not reconnect. The scalar is consumed with its event.

```tsrust
import { SseEvent } from "std:http";

function main() {
  const value: SseEvent = {
    data: 'hello', retryMs: 0
  };
  console.log(value.retryMs);
}
```

Expected output: 0.

HttpSseOptions.documentation:
Optional nonnegative maximum idle interval in milliseconds. Omitted with no text disables keepalive; text alone selects the15-second interval. Zero requests the backend zero interval. An interval outside the timer range throws HttpError code sse during response construction. Options are read and stored independently; no producer is started.

```tsrust
import { SseOptions } from "std:http";

function main() {
  const value: SseOptions = {
    keepAliveMs: 15000
  };
  console.log(value.keepAliveMs);
}
```

Expected output: 15000.

Optional keepalive comment text. Supplying text alone enables a15-second interval; an empty string requests an empty comment. Omitted with an interval selects the empty comment. CR or LF throws HttpError code sse before the response is built. The options string is borrowed and copied into the independent transport setting.

```tsrust
import { SseOptions } from "std:http";

function main() {
  const value: SseOptions = {
    keepAliveText: 'alive'
  };
  console.log(value.keepAliveText);
}
```

Expected output: alive.

HttpWebSocketOptions.documentation:
Optional nonnegative target-representable read-buffer capacity in bytes. Omitted preserves131072 bytes. Zero is accepted by the backend. Invalid values throw HttpError code options before connection or route registration. Configuration is borrowed; each socket owns its buffer.

```tsrust
import { WebSocketOptions } from "std:http";

function main() {
  const value: WebSocketOptions = {
    readBufferSize: 4096
  };
  console.log(value.readBufferSize);
}
```

Expected output: 4096.

Optional nonnegative target-representable write-buffer threshold in bytes. Omitted preserves131072 bytes. send flushes its message before its task succeeds. maxWriteBufferSize must exceed this value. Configuration is borrowed; socket buffers remain exclusive owners.

```tsrust
import { WebSocketOptions } from "std:http";

function main() {
  const value: WebSocketOptions = {
    writeBufferSize: 0
  };
  console.log(value.writeBufferSize);
}
```

Expected output: 0.

Optional write-buffer maximum in bytes. Omitted preserves the target usize maximum; null explicitly requests that same unbounded backend maximum. A supplied integer must be nonnegative, target-representable and greater than writeBufferSize. Violations throw code options. This bounds the backend buffer, not a new facade queue; configuration is borrowed.

```tsrust
import { WebSocketOptions } from "std:http";

function main() {
  const value: WebSocketOptions = {
    maxWriteBufferSize: null
  };
  console.log(value.maxWriteBufferSize);
}
```

Expected output: null.

Optional maximum complete incoming message bytes. Omitted preserves67108864 bytes; null disables this backend bound. Integers must be nonnegative and target-representable; zero permits empty messages only. Oversized input fails receive with code capacity. Configuration is borrowed; no message clone is introduced.

```tsrust
import { WebSocketOptions } from "std:http";

function main() {
  const value: WebSocketOptions = {
    maxMessageSize: 65536
  };
  console.log(value.maxMessageSize);
}
```

Expected output: 65536.

Optional maximum incoming frame bytes. Omitted preserves16777216 bytes; null disables this backend bound. Integers must be nonnegative and target-representable. Exceeding the selected bound fails receive with code capacity. Configuration is borrowed and does not install an application queue.

```tsrust
import { WebSocketOptions } from "std:http";

function main() {
  const value: WebSocketOptions = {
    maxFrameSize: 65536
  };
  console.log(value.maxFrameSize);
}
```

Expected output: 65536.

Optional server policy for unmasked client frames. Omitted or false preserves rejection; true explicitly permits them. This does not change client masking and is not an origin or authentication check. Configuration is borrowed; install authorization before upgrade.

```tsrust
import { WebSocketOptions } from "std:http";

function main() {
  const value: WebSocketOptions = {
    acceptUnmaskedFrames: false
  };
  console.log(value.acceptUnmaskedFrames);
}
```

Expected output: false.

HttpWebSocketClientOptions.documentation:
Optional nonempty PEM CA bundle. Omitted preserves verified public roots. Supplied certificates replace roots for this connection without disabling hostname, chain or validity checks. Invalid PEM throws HttpError code tls. Options remain borrowed until the connect task settles; no key or certificate data is logged.

```tsrust
import { WebSocketClientOptions } from "std:http";

function main() {
  const value: WebSocketClientOptions = {};
  console.log(value.ca);
}
```

Expected output: undefined.

Optional ordered request-header entries, including application authorization or origin. Omitted adds none. Invalid header grammar throws code options; handshake rejection throws a transport error with credentials redacted. These are metadata copies, not payload clones. The options array is borrowed through connect settlement.

```tsrust
import { WebSocketClientOptions } from "std:http";

function main() {
  const value: WebSocketClientOptions = {
    headers: [{
      name: 'origin', value: 'https://app.example'
    }]
  };
  console.log(value.headers !== undefined);
}
```

Expected output: true.

Optional socket buffer/frame/message policy. Omitted preserves every backend default. Invalid ranges throw code options before connecting; null message/frame bounds are explicit unlimited policies. The settings are borrowed until connect settles and the resulting socket owns its configuration.

```tsrust
import { WebSocketClientOptions } from "std:http";

function main() {
  const value: WebSocketClientOptions = {
    socket: {
      readBufferSize: 4096
    }
  };
  console.log(value.socket !== undefined);
}
```

Expected output: true.

HttpWebSocketHeader.documentation:
Required HTTP request-header name. Header grammar is checked during connect; invalid names throw HttpError code options. No application header is added by default. The options record is borrowed and the backend request owns parsed metadata.

```tsrust
import { WebSocketHeader } from "std:http";

function main() {
  const value: WebSocketHeader = {
    name: 'origin', value: 'https://app.example'
  };
