import { ThemeTypography } from 'std:ui';
function main() {
  const typography: ThemeTypography = { base: 16, xl: 24, headingFamily: 'serif' };
  console.log(typography.headingFamily ?? 'sans');
}

std:ui.documentation:
A prop that accepts either a constant or a live expression: `caption="Ready"` or `caption={name.get()}`.

In the component, `const caption = useProp(props.caption)` and `caption.get()` returns the latest value. Records, resources and callbacks cannot be live.

Ownership: the constant or getter moves once into the component.

```tsrx
interface BadgeProps { label: ReactiveValue<string>; }
function Badge(props: BadgeProps): Node {
  const label = useProp(props.label);
  return <Text>{label.get()}</Text>;
}
```

examples.source:
import { useId } from 'std:ui';
function main() {
  const first = useId();
  const second = useId();
  console.log(first === second);
}

std:ui.documentation:
Turns a `ReactiveValue<T>` prop into a value you can read: `const label = useProp(props.caption)`, then `label.get()`.

`get()` returns the latest value without rerunning the component. Only scalar props are supported. Declare it with `const` in the component.

Ownership: the component tree owns the result; bindings do not keep it alive.

```tsrx
function Title(props: { text: ReactiveValue<string> }): Node {
  const text = useProp(props.text);
  return <Text className="text-xl">{text.get()}</Text>;
}
```

Checks the app's GitHub releases (`appInfo().repo`) for a newer version without blocking the window.

`onChecked` receives `update.available` (a newer release exists for this platform) or `update.error` (no network, no repository, rate limited).

```tsrx
checkForUpdates((update) => {
  if (update.available) { notify(`Version ${update.latest} is ready`); }
});
```

The app must be packaged with `tsrust package --repo owner/name`. Requests use the system curl and the public GitHub API, which allows 60 unauthenticated requests per hour per address. Ownership: consumes onChecked, which runs once.

The result of checkForUpdates: current (installed version), latest (the newest release's version, empty when the check failed), available (newer and shipped for this platform), notes (release notes, Markdown) and error (empty on success).

```tsrx
checkForUpdates((update) => {
  status.set(update.available ? `Version ${update.latest} is ready` : 'Up to date');
});
```

Downloads the latest release for this platform, verifies it against the release's `SHA256SUMS`, and replaces the installed app.

The running app keeps its current code until `relaunch()`. On macOS, a signed app accepts only an update signed by the same team. `onInstalled` receives an error message, or an empty string on success.

```tsrx
installUpdate((error) => {
  if (error === '') { relaunch(); } else { notify(error, { variant: 'error' }); }
});
```

The app's folder must be writable: apps installed by a system package manager (such as a .deb) report an error and should update through that manager. Ownership: consumes onInstalled, which runs once.

Registers the messages for one locale; registering it again replaces them.

`messages` is a JSON object, usually imported: `import fr from './locales/fr.json'`. Nested objects give dotted keys (`menu.save`), `{name}` placeholders take values, and a `count` value picks `key_zero`, `key_one` or `key_other`. Lookup tries the exact locale, then its language, then `en`, then shows the key.

```tsrx
import { Text, t, tWith, translateWith, setTranslations, setLocale } from 'std:ui';
import en from './locales/en.json';
import fr from './locales/fr.json';

setTranslations('en', en);
setTranslations('fr', fr);
// <Text>{t('title')}</Text>
// <Text>{tWith('greeting', { name: 'Ada' })}</Text>
// <Text>{translateWith('messages', { count: count.get() })}</Text>
// <Button onPress={() => { setLocale('fr'); }}>Français</Button>
```

Invalid catalogs (not an object, or values other than strings and nested objects) throw. Ownership: messages are read and copied.

Live translated text for `key`, usable as a TSRX child or a string prop. It updates when `setLocale` changes the locale.

Keys use dots for nested messages (`menu.save`). A missing translation falls back to the language, then `en`, then the key itself. Use `translateWith` to fill placeholders.

```tsrx
import { Text, t, tWith, translateWith, setTranslations, setLocale } from 'std:ui';
import en from './locales/en.json';
import fr from './locales/fr.json';

setTranslations('en', en);
setTranslations('fr', fr);
// <Text>{t('title')}</Text>
// <Text>{tWith('greeting', { name: 'Ada' })}</Text>
// <Text>{translateWith('messages', { count: count.get() })}</Text>
// <Button onPress={() => { setLocale('fr'); }}>Français</Button>
```

Registers a GPUI Kit theme set: a name and a themes array, each theme with a name, a mode (light or dark), colors and an optional highlight section for code. Apply one with useTheme. Utility classes such as text-muted-foreground and border-border follow the active theme. An invalid set shows an error notification.

```tsrx
import gruvbox from './themes/gruvbox.json';

function main() {
  registerThemes(gruvbox);
  useTheme('Gruvbox Dark Medium');
  unwrap(run(<App/>, 'Notes'));
}
```

Ownership: the set is read and copied.

Removes the notification shown with this id; nothing happens when none is showing.

```tsrx
notify('Uploading...', { id: 'upload', autohide: false });
dismissNotification('upload');
```

Ownership: arguments are read; nothing is retained after the call except an owned callback, which runs once.

An action for `controlTerminal`.

`focus`, `write` (exact text), `paste` (normalized line endings), `interrupt` (Ctrl+C), `copy`, `copy-output` (scrollback and screen), `scroll`, `select`, `close` (ends the shell and its foreground job) and `restart` (only after the shell has exited). Hiding a `Terminal` does not close it.

Ownership: plain data.

```tsrust
import { TerminalAction } from "std:ui";

function main() {
  const action: TerminalAction = "write";
  console.log(action);
}
```

Expected output: write.

Arguments for `controlTerminal`: the `action`, plus `text` for `write`/`paste` (up to 1 MiB; add `\r` to press Enter), `lines` for `scroll` (positive scrolls up) or `selection` for `select` (`[startRow, startColumn, endRow, endColumn]`).

`expectedGeneration` (from `readTerminal`) makes the action fail if the shell was restarted. Input runs real commands: enforce your own permissions before sending it.

Ownership: the request is queued in the window that sent it.

```tsrust
import { TerminalRequest } from "std:ui";

function main() {
  const request: TerminalRequest = {
    action: "write", text: "pwd\r"
  };
  console.log(request.action);
}
```

Expected output: write.

Asynchronous terminal action outcome. ok=true means the action was delivered, not that a shell command completed or succeeded. ok=false carries error for missing session, unsupported action, invalid arguments or failed PTY input. Example: result.ok=false with error Terminal session is not mounted means the named Terminal has not been displayed. Ownership: copied result data; callbacks borrow it for their duration.

```tsrust
import { TerminalCommandResult } from "std:ui";

function main() {
  const result: TerminalCommandResult = {
    ok: false, error: "Terminal session is not mounted"
  };
  console.log(result.ok);
}
```

Expected output: false.

A copy of a terminal's state from `readTerminal`.

`found` is false for an unknown id; otherwise it has `directory`, `title`, `exited`, `exitCode`, `error`, `text` (the visible screen only), `selectedText`, `columns`, `rows`, `scrollOffset`, `focused` and `generation` (changes on restart). Reading it has no effect on the terminal.

Ownership: an independent copy; later terminal output does not change it.

```tsrust
import { TerminalSnapshot } from "std:ui";

function main() {
  const snapshot: TerminalSnapshot = {
    found: false
  };
  console.log(snapshot.found);
}
```

Expected output: false.

Delivery receipt from answerEditorLanguage. accepted is false for stale, cancelled, expired or other-window requests. Reading the receipt does not edit or focus a document.

```tsrust
import { EditorLanguageDelivery } from "std:ui";

function main() {
  const delivery: EditorLanguageDelivery = {
    accepted: false
  };
  console.log(delivery.accepted);
}
```

Expected output: false.

Applies one language-server completion to a copy of a document and returns the new text. Nothing is edited, focused or saved.

`text` is the current document; `item` is the JSON `CompletionItem`; `start` and `end` are UTF-8 byte offsets used when the item has no `textEdit`. Snippet placeholders are expanded and server commands are ignored. Overlapping or out-of-range edits return `Err`. Check that the document has not changed before applying the result.

```tsr
const proposed = unwrap(completionText('pri', '{"label":"print"}', 0, 3));
console.log(proposed); // print
```

Ownership: reads inputs; returns independent text.

```tsrust
import { completionText } from "std:ui";

function main() {
  console.log(unwrap(completionText("con", JSON.stringify({
    label: "console"
  }), 0, 3)));
}
```

Expected output: console.
